# Covered-A₆ source product geometry

`source_product_geometry` constructs H* ≃ L₃(2) × S₃ from the genuine
earlier natural setup, factorization, normalizer and Fitting clauses,
relative component normality, the source Sylow subgroup, noncontainment,
and the independently supplied K* ≃ L₃(2). It discharges the residual
placement, inner-action and S₃-centralizer premises of the product.

One point-oriented equivalence marks K*, X*, L₀*, L₁*, T*, L₀*T* and
L₁*T*, and all four requested intrinsic two-cores. The actual corrected
inverter in T∩L maps to the specified transposition and centralizes K*.
The full two-core of L₀* is retained. The literal seed satisfies both
commutator identities and the point-residual fixed-space relation.

The tensor adapters use this same equivalence for the cubic actor, point
radical, critical conjugacy and action identities. They preserve the actual
source action and seed. The tensor identification, representation exclusion
and final L₁-containment are separate obligations of the source-theorem owner.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, combined manuscript of 1 March 2004,
13.8.21(1), covered-A₆ paragraph, printed p.957.
-/
